<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97550" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγγρᾰφ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>given to writing</i>, esp. <i>prose works</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιητικὸς ἢ ξ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				35
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.205b
			</span></i>; <i>of</i> or <i>in prose composition</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεινότης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pisc.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετὴ καὶ κακία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
					42
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον εἶδος</span>
			<i>more suited to prose</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.Rh.
				p.411
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
			Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς ἐρεῖν</span> speak
				<i>like a book</i>, i.e. with great precision, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				102d
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπομνηματικῶς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).529
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
